    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0519" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.01/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-06T17:00:00-06:00">January 6, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. My telegram number 2, January 6, 11 a.m., Department’s telegram number 1,
                    January 6, noon.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d420-f1"/> The Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    advises me that conditional upon the call for new elections the Costa Rican
                    Government will extend recognition to the Andrade government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
